cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ADSynth in your work, please cite the DSN 2024 paper listed under
  preferred-citation. Citing this software release as well is welcome.
type: software
title: "ADSynth: A Tool to Synthesize Realistic Active Directory Attack Graphs"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-29
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/AUCyberLab/ADSynth"
url: "https://aucyberlab.github.io/adsynthesizer/"
abstract: >-
  ADSynth generates synthetic Active Directory attack graphs based on
  set-to-set mapping, an intrinsic property of AD systems. It models the
  structure of AD graphs, security permissions and common administration
  misconfigurations following published design guidelines, at security levels
  ranging from vulnerable to extremely secure. It also generates Microsoft
  Entra ID and hybrid identity environments, non-human identities including AI
  agents, and exports to Neo4j JSONL and BloodHound Community Edition OpenGraph.
keywords:
  - active-directory
  - attack-graph
  - bloodhound
  - neo4j
  - entra-id
  - synthetic-data
  - security
